{"slug":"/students/subjects/physics/mechanics/simple-machines-interactive/","source":"students/subjects/physics/mechanics/simple-machines-interactive.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Simple Machines - Physics","description":"","subject":"physics","body":"<!-- Header -->\n    <nav class=\"bg-white shadow-sm fixed top-0 w-full z-50\">\n        <div class=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4\">\n            <div class=\"flex justify-between h-16 items-center\">\n                <div class=\"flex items-center\">\n                    <a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/mechanics/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 mr-4\">\n                        <span class=\"mi -arrow-left\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>\n                    </a>\n                    <h1 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900\">Simple Machines</h1>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"flex items-center space-x-4\">\n                    <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-600 hidden sm:block\">\n                        Progress: <span id=\"progressPercent\">0%</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"w-24 sm:w-32 h-2 bg-gray-200 rounded-full\">\n                        <div id=\"progressBar\" class=\"h-2 bg-blue-500 rounded-full transition-all duration-300\" style=\"width: 0%\"></div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </nav>\n\n    <!-- Main Content -->\n    <main class=\"pt-20 pb-8 px-4 max-w-5xl mx-auto\">\n        <!-- Learning Objectives -->\n        <div class=\"bg-blue-50 border-l-4 border-blue-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6 animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n            <ul class=\"text-blue-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                <li>• Define simple machines and their purpose</li>\n                <li>• Calculate mechanical advantage, velocity ratio, and efficiency</li>\n                <li>• Describe the six types of simple machines</li>\n                <li>• Explain how machines make work easier</li>\n                <li>• Apply simple machine principles to real-world examples</li>\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 1: Introduction -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-blue-100 text-blue-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n                What are Simple Machines?\n            </h2>\n            \n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">A <strong>simple machine</strong> is a device that makes work easier by changing the magnitude or direction of a force. All complex machines are built from combinations of simple machines.</p>\n            \n            <div class=\"bg-amber-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-amber-500 mb-4\">\n                <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-amber-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Key Concept</h4>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">Simple machines do NOT reduce the total work done - they trade off force for distance. The same work is done, but with less effort over a greater distance.</p>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-green-200 text-center\">\n                    <span class=\"mi -cogs text-green-500 text-3xl mb-2\" data-mi=\"settings\">settings</span>\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-700\">What They Do</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">Multiply force, multiply speed, or change direction</p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200 text-center\">\n                    <span class=\"mi -equals text-blue-500 text-3xl mb-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-700\">Energy Conservation</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">Work input = Work output (ideal)</p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-purple-200 text-center\">\n                    <span class=\"mi -list-ol text-purple-500 text-3xl mb-2\" data-mi=\"format_list_numbered\">format_list_numbered</span>\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-700\">Six Types</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">Lever, pulley, inclined plane, wedge, screw, wheel &amp; axle</p>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 2: Key Terms -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-blue-100 text-blue-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n                Key Terms &amp; Calculations\n            </h2>\n\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-orange-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-orange-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-orange-700 mb-2\">Mechanical Advantage (MA)</h4>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg text-center mb-2\">\n                        <p class=\"text-lg font-mono font-bold\">MA = Load / Effort</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">The ratio of output force to input force. Higher MA means less effort needed.</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1\">MA &gt; 1: Force multiplier</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">MA &lt; 1: Speed multiplier</p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-teal-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-teal-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-teal-700 mb-2\">Velocity Ratio (VR)</h4>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg text-center mb-2\">\n                        <p class=\"text-lg font-mono font-bold\">VR = d<sub>E</sub> / d<sub>L</sub></p>\n                    </div>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">The ratio of distance moved by effort to distance moved by load.</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1\">Also: VR = Distance effort / Distance load</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">Or: VR = Speed of effort / Speed of load</p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-indigo-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-indigo-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-indigo-700 mb-2\">Efficiency (η)</h4>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg text-center mb-2\">\n                        <p class=\"text-lg font-mono font-bold\">η = (MA / VR) × 100%</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">How effectively a machine converts input work to output work.</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1\">η is always less than 100% due to friction</p>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -info-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"info\">info</span>Important Relationships</h4>\n                <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                    <li>• <strong>Ideal machine:</strong> MA = VR, Efficiency = 100%</li>\n                    <li>• <strong>Real machines:</strong> MA &lt; VR, Efficiency &lt; 100% (due to friction)</li>\n                    <li>• Work input = Effort × Distance effort moves</li>\n                    <li>• Work output = Load × Distance load moves</li>\n                </ul>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 3: Levers -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-blue-100 text-blue-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n                Levers\n            </h2>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-green-500 mb-4\">\n                <p class=\"text-green-800 font-medium\">A <strong>lever</strong> is a rigid bar that rotates around a fixed point called the fulcrum (pivot). It can multiply force or speed depending on the positions of load, effort, and fulcrum.</p>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-red-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-red-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-red-700 mb-2 text-center\">First Class</h4>\n                    <div class=\"text-center mb-2\">\n                        <span class=\"text-2xl\">⚖️</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm text-center mb-2\">Fulcrum between Load and Effort</p>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded text-xs text-center\">\n                        <strong>Examples:</strong> Seesaw, scissors, crowbar, pliers\n                    </div>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-500 text-xs mt-2 text-center\">MA can be &gt;1, =1, or &lt;1</p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-2 text-center\">Second Class</h4>\n                    <div class=\"text-center mb-2\">\n                        <span class=\"text-2xl\">🛒</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm text-center mb-2\">Load between Fulcrum and Effort</p>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded text-xs text-center\">\n                        <strong>Examples:</strong> Wheelbarrow, bottle opener, nutcracker\n                    </div>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-500 text-xs mt-2 text-center\">MA always &gt; 1 (force multiplier)</p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-purple-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-700 mb-2 text-center\">Third Class</h4>\n                    <div class=\"text-center mb-2\">\n                        <span class=\"text-2xl\">🏏</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm text-center mb-2\">Effort between Fulcrum and Load</p>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded text-xs text-center\">\n                        <strong>Examples:</strong> Fishing rod, tweezers, human arm, broom\n                    </div>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-500 text-xs mt-2 text-center\">MA &lt; 1 (speed multiplier)</p>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n                <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -calculator mr-2\" data-mi=\"calculate\">calculate</span>Lever Calculations</h4>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\"><strong>Velocity Ratio:</strong> VR = distance from effort to fulcrum / distance from load to fulcrum</p>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\"><strong>Law of the Lever:</strong> Effort × Effort arm = Load × Load arm</p>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 4: Pulleys -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-blue-100 text-blue-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">4</span>\n                Pulleys\n            </h2>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-teal-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-teal-500 mb-4\">\n                <p class=\"text-teal-800 font-medium\">A <strong>pulley</strong> is a wheel with a groove around its edge for a rope. Pulleys can change the direction of a force and multiply force when used in systems.</p>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2 text-center\">Single Fixed Pulley</h4>\n                    <div class=\"text-center mb-2 text-4xl\">🚡</div>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• Changes direction of effort</li>\n                        <li>• VR = 1, MA = 1</li>\n                        <li>• No mechanical advantage</li>\n                        <li>• Used for convenience (flagpole, well)</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-green-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-700 mb-2 text-center\">Single Movable Pulley</h4>\n                    <div class=\"text-center mb-2 text-4xl\">⭕</div>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• Pulley moves with the load</li>\n                        <li>• VR = 2, MA ≈ 2</li>\n                        <li>• Doubles the lifting force</li>\n                        <li>• Two rope segments support load</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n                <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -layer-group mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>Block and Tackle (Pulley Systems)</h4>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\">Multiple pulleys combined for greater mechanical advantage:</p>\n                <div class=\"grid grid-cols-4 gap-2 text-sm\">\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded text-center\">\n                        <p class=\"font-medium\">2 pulleys</p>\n                        <p class=\"text-gray-500\">VR = 2</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded text-center\">\n                        <p class=\"font-medium\">3 pulleys</p>\n                        <p class=\"text-gray-500\">VR = 3</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded text-center\">\n                        <p class=\"font-medium\">4 pulleys</p>\n                        <p class=\"text-gray-500\">VR = 4</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded text-center\">\n                        <p class=\"font-medium\">n pulleys</p>\n                        <p class=\"text-gray-500\">VR = n</p>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-500 text-xs mt-2\"><strong>Key:</strong> Count the number of rope segments supporting the load = VR</p>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 5: Inclined Plane & Wedge -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-blue-100 text-blue-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">5</span>\n                Inclined Plane &amp; Wedge\n            </h2>\n\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-orange-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-orange-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-orange-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -ramp-loading mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>Inclined Plane</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\">A flat surface tilted at an angle to the horizontal. Makes lifting easier by increasing distance.</p>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg text-center mb-2\">\n                        <p class=\"font-mono font-bold\">VR = Length / Height = 1 / sin(θ)</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• <strong>Examples:</strong> Ramp, slide, mountain road</li>\n                        <li>• Gentler slope = Higher VR = Less effort needed</li>\n                        <li>• Trade-off: Move load greater distance</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-red-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-red-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-red-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -arrow-down mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_downward\">arrow_downward</span>Wedge</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\">A double inclined plane that moves. Converts input force to splitting force.</p>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg text-center mb-2\">\n                        <p class=\"font-mono font-bold\">VR = Length / Width</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• <strong>Examples:</strong> Axe, knife, chisel, nail</li>\n                        <li>• Longer, thinner wedge = Higher VR</li>\n                        <li>• Force applied to base, work done at tip</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 6: Screw & Wheel and Axle -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-blue-100 text-blue-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">6</span>\n                Screw &amp; Wheel and Axle\n            </h2>\n\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -screwdriver mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>Screw</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\">An inclined plane wrapped around a cylinder. Converts rotational motion to linear motion.</p>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg text-center mb-2\">\n                        <p class=\"font-mono font-bold\">VR = 2πr / p</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-500 text-xs mb-2\">r = radius of handle, p = pitch (distance between threads)</p>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• <strong>Examples:</strong> Bolt, screw jack, drill, jar lid</li>\n                        <li>• Smaller pitch = Higher VR = More force</li>\n                        <li>• Very high mechanical advantage possible</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-indigo-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-indigo-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-indigo-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -circle-notch mr-2\" data-mi=\"pending\">pending</span>Wheel and Axle</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\">A larger wheel attached to a smaller axle. Both rotate together.</p>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg text-center mb-2\">\n                        <p class=\"font-mono font-bold\">VR = R / r</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-500 text-xs mb-2\">R = radius of wheel, r = radius of axle</p>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• <strong>Examples:</strong> Steering wheel, doorknob, wrench</li>\n                        <li>• Larger wheel relative to axle = Higher VR</li>\n                        <li>• Can multiply force or speed</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 7: PhET Simulation -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-blue-100 text-blue-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">7</span>\n                Interactive Simulation: Balancing Act\n            </h2>\n            \n            <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n                <div class=\"simulation-container\">\n                    <iframe src=\"https://phet.colorado.edu/sims/html/balancing-act/latest/balancing-act_en.html\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen=\"\"></iframe>\n                </div>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-500 text-sm mt-2 text-center\"><span class=\"mi -info-circle mr-1\" data-mi=\"info\">info</span>Explore how levers work by balancing different masses. Try moving the fulcrum to change the mechanical advantage!</p>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 8: Video -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-blue-100 text-blue-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">8</span>\n                Video: Simple Machines Explained\n            </h2>\n            \n            <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n                <div class=\"video-container\">\n                    <iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/lRuZm4Q-R5U\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen=\"\"></iframe>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 9: Practice Problems -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-blue-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>\n                Practice Questions\n            </h2>\n\n            <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. A lever has an effort arm of 80 cm and a load arm of 20 cm. Calculate the velocity ratio and the effort needed to lift a 200 N load.</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            <strong>Velocity Ratio:</strong><br>\n                            VR = Effort arm / Load arm = 80 / 20 = <strong>4</strong><br><br>\n                            <strong>Effort (assuming 100% efficiency):</strong><br>\n                            MA = VR = 4<br>\n                            Effort = Load / MA = 200 / 4 = <strong>50 N</strong>\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. A pulley system has 4 pulleys. Calculate the effort required to lift a 600 N load if the system is 75% efficient.</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            <strong>Velocity Ratio:</strong> VR = 4 (4 pulleys)<br><br>\n                            <strong>Mechanical Advantage:</strong><br>\n                            Efficiency = MA / VR<br>\n                            0.75 = MA / 4<br>\n                            MA = 3<br><br>\n                            <strong>Effort:</strong><br>\n                            Effort = Load / MA = 600 / 3 = <strong>200 N</strong>\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. An inclined plane is 5 m long and 1 m high. Calculate its velocity ratio. If a 100 N effort moves a 400 N load up the ramp, what is the efficiency?</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            <strong>Velocity Ratio:</strong><br>\n                            VR = Length / Height = 5 / 1 = <strong>5</strong><br><br>\n                            <strong>Mechanical Advantage:</strong><br>\n                            MA = Load / Effort = 400 / 100 = 4<br><br>\n                            <strong>Efficiency:</strong><br>\n                            η = (MA / VR) × 100% = (4 / 5) × 100% = <strong>80%</strong>\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">4. A wheel and axle has a wheel radius of 30 cm and an axle radius of 5 cm. Calculate the VR. If an effort of 50 N is applied, what load can be lifted (assuming 80% efficiency)?</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            <strong>Velocity Ratio:</strong><br>\n                            VR = R / r = 30 / 5 = <strong>6</strong><br><br>\n                            <strong>Mechanical Advantage:</strong><br>\n                            η = MA / VR<br>\n                            0.8 = MA / 6<br>\n                            MA = 4.8<br><br>\n                            <strong>Load:</strong><br>\n                            Load = MA × Effort = 4.8 × 50 = <strong>240 N</strong>\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Key Takeaways -->\n        <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-50 to-indigo-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-blue-200 animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways</h3>\n            <ul class=\"text-blue-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n                <li>• Six simple machines: Lever, pulley, inclined plane, wedge, screw, wheel &amp; axle</li>\n                <li>• MA = Load / Effort; VR = Distance effort / Distance load; η = (MA/VR) × 100%</li>\n                <li>• Machines trade force for distance - same work, easier to do</li>\n                <li>• Real machines always have η &lt; 100% due to friction</li>\n                <li>• Count rope segments in pulley systems to find VR</li>\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Navigation -->\n        <div class=\"flex justify-between items-center mt-8\">\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/mechanics/friction/\" class=\"px-4 py-2 text-gray-600 hover:text-gray-900\">\n                <span class=\"mi -chevron-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"chevron_left\">chevron_left</span>Previous\n            </a>\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/mechanics/work-energy-power/\" class=\"px-4 py-2 bg-blue-500 text-white rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-600\">\n                Next: Work, Energy &amp; Power<span class=\"mi -chevron-right ml-2\" data-mi=\"chevron_right\">chevron_right</span>\n            </a>\n        </div>\n    </main>\n\n    \n\n<!-- Topic Quiz System -->","bodyClass":"bg-gray-50 min-h-screen","bodyStyle":"","css":["@keyframes fade-in-up {\n            from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(20px); }\n            to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }\n        }\n        .animate-fade-in-up { animation: fade-in-up 0.5s ease-out forwards; }\n        .section-card {\n            background: white;\n            border-radius: 12px;\n            padding: 1.5rem;\n            margin-bottom: 1.5rem;\n            box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);\n            border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;\n        }\n        .video-container {\n            position: relative;\n            width: 100%;\n            padding-bottom: 56.25%;\n            height: 0;\n            overflow: hidden;\n            border-radius: 8px;\n            background: #f9fafb;\n        }\n        .video-container iframe {\n            position: absolute;\n            top: 0; left: 0;\n            width: 100%;\n            height: 100%;\n            border: none;\n        }\n        .simulation-container {\n            position: relative;\n            width: 100%;\n            padding-bottom: 60%;\n            height: 0;\n            overflow: hidden;\n            border-radius: 8px;\n            background: #f9fafb;\n        }\n        .simulation-container iframe {\n            position: absolute;\n            top: 0; left: 0;\n            width: 100%;\n            height: 100%;\n            border: none;\n        }"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}